save(HERE/'template-extraction.json',{'basis':g.CAP['basis'],'source_descriptions':rows,'choice_mapping':'source-bank-replay.json assigns every original option to its field, exact vector and recipe, or records original-only unresolved values','backbone':'3x3 integer matrix times length-3 column; three ordered row dot products, three expanded dot sums, evaluated product sums, final column. Named/inline prompts and radio/3-blank contracts remain separate.','fixed':{'shape':'3x3 by 3x1','row_order':'All three output rows in supplied order','operation':'matrix-column multiplication','solution_stages':['expand three dot products','evaluate individual signed products','sum each row'],'field_contracts':{'radio':'one selection field, five whole-vector choices','blank':'field-1/2/3 are the first/second/third output integers'}},'slots':{'A':'all nine integer entries, independently sampled -8..8','v':'all three entries -8..8; not all zero','matrix_name':['A','B','L','P','N','Z'],'vector_name':['x','y','z','v','n']},'generalizations':'Independent entry sampling preserves the nine-product method. Zero/repeated rows, matching outputs and signed values are allowed for blanks. Whole-vector radio banks reject any duplicate options. Special repeated-row source examples do not impose a different operation. Name changes do not establish distinctness.','sampling_bounds_reason':'Conservative interval covers every observed source coefficient/vector coordinate; no added stages, fractions or difficulty relabeling.','domains':'Integers; exact finite multiplication, no branch restrictions; exclude all-zero vector as a narrower instructional policy.','profiles':{mid:[{'recipe':r,'observed_vector':x} for r,x in g.bank(mid,g.parameters(q))] for mid,q in g.SOURCES.items() if g.template_of(mid).endswith('radio')},'excluded_profiles':g.EXCLUDED,'notation_correction':'Historical choices use doubled escapes for begin/end and rows; generation emits one LaTeX command escape and standard double-backslash rows. No source record is edited.','fidelity_limits':'Decorative alignment spacing is simplified. Unresolved choice banks replay observed data at original parameters only; excluded from generalized fidelity claims.'})
(HERE/'template-extraction.md').write_text('''# Multiplying a 3×3 matrix by a column vector

The supplied matrix and vector determine all three output entries. Multiply corresponding row/vector entries, display the three signed products in each row, and add those products. Keep row order and the three-stage solution sequence.

There are four complete moderate templates: named matrix/vector with one five-choice radio field; inline product with the same field; named matrix/vector with three scalar blanks in the source table; and inline product with three scalar blanks in the source table. The incomplete “What is” source is recorded separately.

Each of the nine matrix entries and three vector entries is a declared integer slot. The observed values all fit −8 through 8. Sampling these slots independently is a same-method generalization; repeated or zero source entries are observations, not necessary constraints. All-zero vectors are omitted by a narrower sampling policy. Names can change throughout prompt and solution but do not create new mathematical tasks. Entire ordered output vectors remain the target; there is no queried-position slot.

Every supported radio profile is chosen as a whole bank. With correct vector (r,t,u), profiles use documented coordinate negation, coordinate swaps, or (r,r,−u). See the exact per-choice mappings and formulas in source-bank-replay.json and the generator's bank function. No partial bank is pooled with another. Duplicate values reject the instance.

q-77349 and q-77351 contain irregular banks with unresolved interpretations. Their original banks are retained and replayed at original parameters, but are excluded from generalized sampling. Their canonical keys and worked solutions still pass independent mathematics and native ID grading. q-13557 and q-13558 lack ratings, keys, and solutions; they do not contribute to inventory.

The original blank keys and table placements are retained, including field-2 belonging to the middle row regardless of entity ordering. Generated answers are delimiter-free integers. Named and inline solutions retain expanded products, evaluated product sums, and the final output. Decorative spacing is simplified; no stages are removed.

Practice material uses LaTeX only. The two canonical image assets were visually inspected and are standalone rendered matrix notation, so no plot extraction or rendering is needed. Originals and their asset bytes remain unchanged.
''')
